        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ぜったい",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ぜったい — zettai — \"absolutely; definitely\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "あぶないから、ぜったい いかないで ください。 — abunai kara, zettai ikanaide kudasai — \"It's dangerous, so do not go there under any circumstances.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ぜったい (zettai) is Sino-Japanese (kango): two Chinese characters read with their on'yomi, readings borrowed from Chinese. They are zetsu, \"cut off\" (Middle Chinese dzjwet) and tai, \"opposite\" (twojH) (KANJIDIC2; Middle Chinese in Baxter's transcription). The two join as zet-tai."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
